>
	<p>
    Hi, I&rsquo;m Ahmad Raza. I&rsquo;m a software engineer who builds web applications.
    I started pursuing a career in this field while I was still in the first year of
    my undergraduate studies. My journey began with building MEAN stack applications as an
    independent freelancer, and I later worked with professional teams to build more complex
    applications.
	</p>

	<p>
    I possess hands-on experience with a variety of technologies, from essentials like
    HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, and TypeScript, through frameworks and platforms such as
    Angular and Fastify, to complementary technologies such as Nix and Terraform.
	</p>


	<p>
    As an individual freelancer, I have worked on platforms like Fiverr and Upwork.
    I consistently maintain ratings above 4.5 on these platforms, along with
    numerous positive reviews from my clients. Since these platforms build
    trust between freelancers and clients &hyphen; I generally prefer working through them.
	</p>

	<p>
    Apart from freelancing, I&rsquo;ve also worked with teams and organizations.
    From Jan 2022 to Oct 2026, I&rsquo;ve held software engineering roles at
    MicroAgility Services, FutureNow Technologies, PieCyfer, and Amaizing. I&rsquo;m
    glad that my former teammates still remember me for my professionalism and expertise.
	</p>

  <p>
    One of my hobbies is engineering within the Linux ecosystem, particularly Nix and NixOS
    in recent years. I like to customize my experience by using reproducible approaches to system
    and software installations. I enjoy customization as a hobby and maintain my own
    configurations, small programs and plugins.
  </p>

  <h2>Personal Life</h2>
  <p>
    In my personal life, I love nature and prefer living in a village with my family.
    I enjoy the company of kids, family members, and others with a good sense of humor.
    I like organic food, including vegetables, seeds, meat and wheat.
  </p>
